omp-fusion
==========

This project is an independent, OMP-native (oh-my-pi / `omp`) port of the
**Fusion-Fable** Claude Code skill by duolahypercho:

    https://github.com/duolahypercho/fusion-fable   (MIT)

What is preserved from the original (the method, credited to duolahypercho):
  - "independence, then synthesis": a panel of models answers the same prompt
    in parallel, blind to one another, then a judge synthesizes.
  - the judge classifies the deliverable and follows one of two tracks:
      Track A — artifact: run, merge, verify
      Track B — research: structured synthesis (consensus / contradictions /
                partial coverage / unique insights / blind spots)
  - no personas / "lenses"; the verbatim task goes to every panelist.

What changed for OMP (this port):
  - Proposers, critics, and the aggregator are ordinary OMP subagents (the
    `task`/`eval` `agent()` path + custom `fusion-proposer` / `fusion-aggregator`
    agents for Fusion, and dedicated `ultrafusion-proposer` / `ultrafusion-critic`
    / `ultrafusion-aggregator` agents for the companion Ultrafusion planning
    pipeline), not Claude Code `Agent` subagents or external CLIs.
  - No `run_codex.sh` / `run_gemini.sh` / `agy` shell runners and no
    `command -v` CLI detection. Any provider/model is selectable through OMP's
    native model resolution.
  - Proposer and aggregator models are configurable via `modelRoles` (`proposer_1..N`,
    `aggregator`) or a per-invocation `--proposers`/`--aggregator` override — the way
    `/advisor`'s model is configured — instead of being pinned to specific model
    versions. These canonical keys are shared: Fusion, Fusion-fast, and Fusion-samp
    all read them, and Ultrafusion reads the same `proposer_1..N`/`aggregator` for its
    own proposer and aggregator waves (adding its own `critic_1..3` for the extra
    critic wave, and its own optional `ultra_aggregator` key — checked before the
    shared `aggregator`, letting Ultrafusion use a different synthesizer than Fusion
    without an equivalent override on the Fusion side).
  - The aggregator is a separate subagent with its own required, configurable model — there
    is no implicit default; it must be set explicitly, independent of the session model.

